  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anil Kumar And Another vs State Of U.P. And Another on 22 May, 2024 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc:93038 Court No. - 92 Case :- Application U/S 482 No. - 14290 of 2024 Applicant :- Anil Kumar And Another Opposite Party :- State of U.P. and Another Counsel for Applicant :- Rahul Kumar Tiwari,Sanjay Kr. Srivastava Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Arun Kumar Singh Deshwal,J. 1. Heard Sri Sanjay Kr. Srivastava, learned counsel for the applicants and Sri Rajeev Kumar, learned AGA for the State. 2. The instant application under Section 482 Cr.P.C. has been filed for quashing the summoning order dated 27.02.2024 as well as entire proceeding of Complaint Case No.901 of 2024 under Sections 26, 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, Police Station- Karari, District Kaushambi pending in the court of Chief Judicial Magistrate Kaushambi. Anil Kumar And Another vs State Of U.P. And Another on 22 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/3830549/ 1 4.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "3. Contention of the learned counsel for the applicants is that as per Section 44 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, sample should have been sent within 14 days but it was sent beyond 14 days. There is a violation of Section 44 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, therefore, impugned proceeding is deserved to be [LEAKAGE_MASK] on this ground."
  },
